><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{B} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></em> and hence <em data-effect="italics"><span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Φ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Φ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{Φ} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></em> when opening and closing the switch in his apparatus (shown in <a href="23-1-induced-emf-and-magnetic-flux#import-auto-id1169738208118" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 23.3">Figure 23.3</a>). This is also true for the bar magnet and coil shown in <a href="23-1-induced-emf-and-magnetic-flux#import-auto-id1169738076827" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 23.4">Figure 23.4</a>. When rotating the coil of a generator, the angle <span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{θ} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span> and, hence, <em data-effect="italics"><span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Φ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Φ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{Φ} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></em> is changed. Just how great an emf and what direction it takes depend on the change in <em data-effect="italics"><span class="os-math-in-para"><math display="inline"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Φ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Φ</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="StarMath 5.0"> size 12{Φ} {}</annotation></semantics></annotation-xml></semantics></math></span></em> and how rapidly the change is made, as examined in the next section.</p>





        
        

        
        
        
        
        
        
     
     
  </div>
  
